  "body": "Imported events must retain editorial changes across later provider refreshes. PR464 records field ownership but its internal metadata is rejected by the current public projections and database visibility filters, and lifecycle reconciliation can overwrite editorial visibility, ticket links and workflow state.\n\nThis replacement preserves PR464\u2019s complete history and normally merges current main. The stored-data boundary recognizes object-valued `_discoveryOwned` evidence, while public requests retain their strict allowlists and responses omit the private key. Editorial updates and image uploads retain unchanged ownership under the event lock and relinquish changed fields permanently. Provider and subscription reconciliation share the same ownership rules, including conservative treatment of legacy rows and fail-closed hiding when a source disappears.\n\nSupersedes #464 after successful integration; original PR and branch remain open/intact until then. Its native stack (#466) cannot be normally merged without GitHub\u2019s history-rewriting stack operation, so this is a standalone history-preserving replacement. #469 already integrated the source/run boundary prerequisites. Original contributor attribution remains in the commit ancestry.\n\nValidation is still in progress locally. Do not merge this draft until the completed results below, hosted checks, independent approval and all review discussions are satisfied.\n\n- Passed repository quality, formal verification, specification inventory and strict catalog gate (1,162 reviewed candidates).\n- Added regression coverage for both database predicates, public projection and request boundaries, editorial image writes, provider/subscription reconciliation, legacy values and QuickCheck ownership invariants.\n- Passed: ten PostgreSQL visibility cases against a disposable native PostgreSQL16 database using the exact extracted current predicate and helpers. This supplements, rather than replaces, the compiled handler tests.\n- Pending: complete prescribed Stack build/test and compiled PostgreSQL predicate/concurrency execution.\n\nNo schema, API shape, source activation or deployment change. The public ownership namespace remains rejected. No force push, original-branch rewrite or protection bypass.\n",
